 # Changelog
 
+## Unreleased (1.5.0)
+
+- Due times: each ticket is due its creation time plus the response time of its priority (urgent 4 hours, high 24,
+  normal 72, low 168; `DUE_HOURS_URGENT`, `DUE_HOURS_HIGH`, `DUE_HOURS_NORMAL`, `DUE_HOURS_LOW` change them). The due
+  time is set once and stored in the data file; tickets already in the file get theirs when the service first starts
+  on it. `GET /tickets?overdue=true` lists the open and in-progress tickets that are past due.
+  **Off until `DUE_TIMES=on`**: until then the API answers exactly as in 1.4.0 (no `due`, `overdue` ignored). Roll out in
+  two steps: deploy 1.5.0, then, once the data file holds the due times, set `DUE_TIMES=on`
+  ([decision 9](docs/decisions/0009-due-times.md)).
+- The data file stays version 1 and release 1.4.0 can still start on a file 1.5.0 wrote (see
+  [operations](docs/operations.md#rolling-back-to-140)).
+
+- `POST /tickets/import` creates up to 5000 tickets at once, all or none, for the move from the old tracker.
+- Ticket assignment: `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee`, an `assignee` on every ticket, the `assignee` filter of `GET /tickets`
+  and `list --assignee`; the agent is notified (`ticket.assigned`). `list --raw` gains the assignee as its last column.
+- `GET /tickets` filters now combine: a ticket must match every filter given, as the API docs always said.
+
 ## 1.4.0 (2025-09-15)
 
 - The operator command line, `bin/tickets.js` (`list`, `show`), and the weekly report, `scripts/weekly-report.js`.
